\C{} Advise on usage of RxDOS version 7.20N

Do not use RxDOS version 7.20N. It tries to re-produce every bug of RxDOS 7.1.5
(as found on the FreeDOS mirrors). It is not usable currently. The release of
version 7.20N is only intended for developers.

\H{} Developing RxDOS

\n Do not take anything for granted.

\n Read and understand all the source code that you use from this release
 before claiming it works.

\n You can read the book \q{Dissecting DOS} for some advise on RxDOS's
internal structure, although it describes an older version. You will need
a deeper understanding for development though.

\n As described in \k{build} the build process currently uses tools
that run and build on DOS, are considered non-free, or require non-free programs
to build. Modifying the kernel and RxCMD to build using nothing but NASM should
be trivial for developers.
